{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgwgbup4mr","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"notifyChange ws-tagging built but no producer emits tagged events yet","summary":"In the per-repo-daemon feature, task #3 added notifyChange(ws?) with a tagged `data: changed:<ws>` payload and a matching graph.html EventSource consumer that skips refetches when the tagged workspace does not match the selected WS. The consumer half and the function are correct and tested. BUT no producer anywhere in the feature branch passes a ws argument — every notifyChange() call in daemon.js AND in all routes/* handlers is bare, so only legacy `data: changed` is ever emitted and the per-ws skip optimization is dormant (never wrongly suppresses; back-compat intact). This is correct + safe, not a defect: the #5 spec said \"only targetOverlay-based write sites pass T.ws\", and those sites live in routes/* which task #3 was forbidden to touch (#4's territory, already merged). The producer wiring (pass T.ws at route-handler notifyChange sites in routes/exec.js, git.js, overlay.js, task.js, session.js, judge.js, etc.) is a follow-up that belongs in a routes-scoped task to actually realize the bandwidth optimization.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T17:11:59.233Z","vec":[-0.10689659416675568,-0.03501782566308975,0.008132632821798325,0.07438258826732635,0.13769900798797607,-0.07341508567333221,0.05946165323257446,-0.044744979590177536,0.049840644001960754,0.08102989941835403,0.0014404894318431616,-0.0051102666184306145,0.012779805809259415,-0.018719203770160675,-0.03115350566804409,0.022219598293304443,0.1148284375667572,-0.07059264183044434,-0.07432310283184052,-0.04426698759198189,0.0028532291762530804,-0.00021725734404753894,0.035287536680698395,0.04923189803957939,0.007070011459290981,-0.0365731455385685,-0.08989038318395615,-0.0062913671135902405,0.0024280683137476444,-0.031070563942193985,0.013154495507478714,0.023474402725696564,-0.1414753943681717,-0.047457292675971985,0.02497079409658909